                  { elem: "M", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "DC : CE = L : M", ref: "VI.12" }] },
            { text: "Then the ratios of {K} to {L} and of {L} to {M} are the same as the ratios of the sides,",
              visible: SETM,
              highlighted: ["K","L","M"] },
            { text: "namely of {BC} to {CG} and of {DC} to {CE}.",
              visible: SETM,
              highlighted: ["BC","CG","DC","CE"] },
            { text: "But the ratio of {K} to {M} is compounded of the ratio of {K} to {L} and of that of {L} to {M},",
              visible: SETM,
              highlighted: ["K","L","M"] },
            { text: "so that {K} has also to {M} the ratio compounded of the ratios of the sides.",
              visible: SETM,
              highlighted: ["K","M","BC","CG","DC","CE"] },
            { text: "Now since {BC} is to {CG} as the parallelogram {AC} is to the parallelogram {CH},",
